> but what changed between 1.14.4 and 1.15.0-pre.2?

tl;dr: a lot. These rules used to be installed/removed by a shell script with a bunch of `ip rule .. || true` that swept all these errors under the rug. Fortunately, this is no longer the case. :)

@reporter I've put up https://github.com/cilium/cilium/pull/29311 that ignores only the specific EAFNOSUPPORT returned by the rule removal. Feel free to play around with this on your own. Are WSL2 kernels typically built with v6 disabled? In this case, you'll need to disable Cilium's v6 support. Otherwise, you'll just hit errors elsewhere.

@participant1's suggestion above may also prove useful. Did you explicitly disable `CONFIG_IPV6_MULTIPLE_TABLES`? I can't figure out from the kernel docs whether this defaults to true or not, but it's pulled in by at least CONFIG_IPV6_SEG6_LWTUNNEL. Unfortunately, there are many places returning EAFNOSUPPORT.
